Lua sandbox hardening: readonly tables, protected globals, eval function in registry, stack cleanup

Redis 6.2.7 fixed two Lua sandbox weaknesses. CVE-2022-24736: a script could
crash the server via an assert reached by passing thousands of arguments to
redis.call (Lua stack exhausted; fixed by popping the call arguments before the
reply is pushed). CVE-2022-24735: a script could inject Lua code that ran at
compile time and override the wrapped f_<sha> global of another script; fixed by
loading the user chunk directly and storing it in the Lua registry, making the
global table and every table reachable from it readonly (new
lua_enablereadonlytable API), installing an allow list for globals created
during initialisation and an __index error metatable for unknown globals, while
keeping print available to avoid a breaking change.

Tracker: CVE-2022-24736 CVE-2022-24735
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/13c1e1f2986adcd8788f464a1931cdfe744f15f9
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/21414ad4802659eeb3e81d20d86b437d3ab882dc
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/b2ce3719afe5440b010ab3f12d9ad35b79cee55a
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/11b602fbf8f9cdf8fc741c24625ab6287ab998a9
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/afb48c6cc971c82f271cf1472638e1e75e09fd56
Upstream patch: https://github.com/redis/redis/commit/93c1d31d97a995cd07a2c235b7a4e177f3c752cc
Adaptation: src/scripting.c hunks re-targeted to KeyDB's src/scripting.cpp (C++17):
 allow-list arrays declared const char * / const char ** and iterated with
 const char *** (string literals are not char* in C++); luaL_loadbuffer takes
 (const char*)ptrFromObj(body) instead of body->ptr; g_pserver-> instead of
 server.; KeyDB's per-thread lua_client setup block left untouched. "keydb" added
 to redis_api_allow_list because KeyDB aliases the redis table as a second
 global (lua_setglobal(lua,"keydb")) that the upstream list does not know.
 "__redis__compare_helper" added to the same list: KeyDB still defines and uses
 it in luaSortArray, and upstream 6.2.7 shipped a startup warning for this very
 global (removed as dead code only in 6.2.8, redis/redis#10701). The unrelated
 6.2.7 hunk adding the min-replicas-to-write check (redis 34505d26f) is not part
 of this series and was not ported. deps/lua/src/* and tests/unit/scripting.tcl
 hunks apply verbatim (KeyDB's copies are identical to Redis 6.2.6).

